    evidence: "inferred",
    title: "The Tamil house and its old people",
    text: "A Chola-era village house was a low mud or brick building around a small open court, with a raised verandah (thinnai) on the street where men sat and guests slept, a kitchen at the back, and a room for grain. Women rose early to sweep the threshold and draw a kolam in rice flour, pounded paddy, cooked rice, kuzhambu and greens on a clay stove, and fetched water from the tank. Houses and fields passed from father to sons, with elder sons often managing for younger brothers. Old parents lived with a son; inscriptions show children giving temple lamps and land in their parents' names, earning merit for them.",
