    text: "Ranjit Singh's kingdom was governed from the darbar at Lahore, where the Maharaja sat with ministers such as the Dogra brothers and Fakir Azizuddin, and Persian remained the language of records. In the districts, kardars collected revenue, judged disputes and kept order, often farming the revenue for a fixed sum. Village headmen (chaudhris, lambardars) and panchayats handled most local matters. The Fauj-i-Khas, trained by European officers in the French manner, and a large army swallowed much of the revenue. Lahore's kotwal kept the city's watch and markets, and the Maharaja's charitable gifts to shrines of all faiths were public acts.",
